# The LFO (0x22: enable bit 3, rate 0-7): a carrier with AM enabled at AMS 3
# and PMS 7 through every rate; then at rate 5, PMS 0 to 7 and AMS 0 to 3;
# PM at a high and a low frequency number and at block 0 and 7 on three more
# channels; the LFO disabled, where the AM offset sits at its maximum, 0x3F
# (an operator with AM enabled is attenuated); and AM enabled on one
# operator of a two-carrier connection only. Re-enabling restarts the
# counter.
